<#times-by-precision> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "times-by-precision" ;
  rdfs:comment "Each time at the precision it is written: a birth time and an immunization to the month as xsd:gYearMonth, a medication's start in a year as xsd:gYear, a problem from a year to a month, and three times short of the second padded to it, each beside a node keeping the characters written: a medication's end at an hour with no offset, a procedure at an hour with one, and a result at a minute with none." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/times-by-precision.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/times-by-precision.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/times-by-precision.ttl>
  ] .

<#null-flavors-not-listed> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "null-flavors-not-listed" ;
  rdfs:comment "The null-flavors document with a nullFlavor that is no NullFlavor code wherever a time would be: a birth time, an immunization's time, a medication's end, a problem's onset, a procedure's time and a result's time, and a result value's. No reason is carried for any of them, and each is a finding, ccda:nullFlavorNotListed, valued by the nullFlavor as written." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/null-flavors-not-listed.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/null-flavors-not-listed.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/null-flavors-not-listed.ttl>
  ] .

<#null-flavors> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "null-flavors" ;
  rdfs:comment "Each null flavour where a value or a time would be is the reason that property is absent, a node of the version naming it and the NullFlavor code: a birth time UNK, an immunization's time NI, a medication's end UNK beside its start, another's whole time UNK, which is its start of use, a problem's onset ASKU, a result's value MSK, so it has no value kind, and a result's time NAV beside its value; a result value's nullFlavor XYZ, no NullFlavor code, is carried as nothing and is a finding." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/null-flavors.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/null-flavors.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/null-flavors.ttl>
  ] .

<#concern-status-beside-a-problem-status> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "concern-status-beside-a-problem-status" ;
  rdfs:comment "One problem states its status in a Problem Status Observation and another does not: the other's concern act status, completed, maps to no clinical status and is a finding, whatever the first problem states." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/concern-status-beside-a-problem-status.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/concern-status-beside-a-problem-status.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/concern-status-beside-a-problem-status.ttl>
  ] .

<#patient-deceased> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "patient-deceased" ;
  rdfs:comment "A patient whose death indicator is true and whose death time is a day: the version holds deceased true, the date of death as an xsd:date, and the administrative gender F mapped by C-CDA on FHIR's concept map to female." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/patient-deceased.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/patient-deceased.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/patient-deceased.ttl>
  ] .

<#patient-gender-and-death-edges> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "patient-gender-and-death-edges" ;
  rdfs:comment "Six patients, one way of stating gender and death each. UN maps to other, the map's wider row, and a death time with a value beside a false indicator is a death, its date a month. A null flavour UNK on the gender is the reason it is absent, and a null flavour on the death time beside a true indicator is the reason the date of death is absent. A gender code U, outside the map, is carried as nothing and is a finding, ccda:administrativeGenderNotMapped, and a null-flavoured indicator and time state no death, so nothing is carried for either. A false indicator alone is deceased false, and M is male. A null flavour that is no NullFlavor code on the gender and on the death time, beside a true indicator, is carried as nothing and is a finding, ccda:nullFlavorNotListed, for each. M in another code system is carried as nothing and is a finding, ccda:administrativeGenderNotMapped, and an indicator padded with spaces, \" true \", is a true indicator." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/patient-gender-and-death-edges.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/patient-gender-and-death-edges.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/patient-gender-and-death-edges.ttl>
  ] .

<#codes-in-other-systems> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "codes-in-other-systems" ;
  rdfs:comment "A drug coded by a formulary's code with an RxNorm translation, a problem coded in ICD-9-CM with a SNOMED CT translation, a procedure coded in HCPCS with CPT and SNOMED CT translations, and a test coded by a lab's local code with a LOINC translation. Each code in a system its kind has a term for is that term's IRI, the CPT code under Cascade's CPT stem; every other is a literal on its kind's cascade:medicationCodeInOtherSystem, conditionCodeInOtherSystem, procedureCodeInOtherSystem or testCodeInOtherSystem, typed by the system's FHIR URI where the code system table lists its OID (ICD-9-CM, HCPCS Level II) and by urn:oid: and the OID where it does not, and none is a finding." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/codes-in-other-systems.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/codes-in-other-systems.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/codes-in-other-systems.ttl>
  ] .

<#result-interpretation-in-another-system> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "result-interpretation-in-another-system" ;
  rdfs:comment "A result flagged L in HL7 Table 0078 with a translation into HL7 ObservationInterpretation. The translation is carried, as the cascade:resultInterpretationCode L, and the flag in Table 0078 is not carried and is a finding, ccda:codeNotCarried." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/result-interpretation-in-another-system.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/result-interpretation-in-another-system.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/result-interpretation-in-another-system.ttl>
  ] .

<#allergy-codes-in-other-systems> a bridge:IsomorphicConversionTest ;
  mf:name "allergy-codes-in-other-systems" ;
  rdfs:comment "An allergy to penicillin coded in RxNorm, with translations in HCPCS Level II, HL7 ObservationInterpretation and ICD-9-CM: only the RxNorm code is carried, as the allergenCode, as before any other code system was added to the table, and each translation is the finding ccda:codeSystemNotMapped, since an allergen is never carried in another code system." ;
  mf:action [
    bridge:input <in/allergy-codes-in-other-systems.xml> ;
    bridge:envelope <../ro-crate-metadata.json#envelope-document> ;
    bridge:facts <facts/portal-download.ttl>
  ] ;
  mf:result [
    bridge:expectedGraph <expected/allergy-codes-in-other-systems.ttl> ;
    bridge:expectedFindings <findings/allergy-codes-in-other-systems.ttl>
  ] .

